#. type: Title #
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:1
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notification and reminder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:8
msgid ""
"Cross-cutting aspect for **durable inbox items**, **scheduled reminders**, "
"and **local interrupts** (companion bubble / OS alert). Sibling to the "
"[Portal data plane](portal-data-plane.md) (live channels) and [page refresh]"
"(page-refresh.md) (no global list polling for attention)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:10
msgid ""
"This is **not** a product module. Feature modules (task, chat, pomodoro, "
"notification UI) link here when they fire attention events."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three concepts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept                     | Meaning                                                   | Persistence                             | Client delivery                                                            |\n"
"| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Notification**            | Inbox row: listable, mark-read, owned by a subject        | PG (`notification*`)                    | Habitat RPC WS `notification.created` (may also trigger a local interrupt) |\n"
"| **Reminder**                | “Ring once at this time” intent; a task may have **many** | On the domain entity (not an Inbox row) | Lightweight WS event → **only** local interrupt                            |\n"
"| **Local interrupt (Alert)** | Channel: companion bubble or OS notification              | Not in PG; device-local                 | `deliverLocalReminder` (`portal-sdk`)                                      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:20
msgid ""
"Companion speech bubble is the preferred **Alert** channel on desktop when "
"the companion window is visible. Bubble click is **not** Inbox ack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:22
msgid ""
"Code namespaces today: Inbox = `notification*`; interrupt = `alert*` / "
"`deliverLocalReminder`. Reminder (product) is the scheduled intent; do not "
"conflate it with Inbox."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "World ownership"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:26
msgid ""
"Deliver notifications to the **subject of the World that owns the entity**. "
"Do not hard-code “user only / never agent”. A `task_item` in the agent World "
"fires a due **Notification** to the agent subject; the same rule applies to "
"the user World."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Task rules (target)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Event                                            | Notification (Inbox)       | Reminder → Alert                               |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Task **due**                                     | Yes (that World’s subject) | May also interrupt via `notification.created`  |\n"
"| Advance reminders (e.g. 7d / 3d / 1d before due) | **No**                     | **Yes** only                                   |\n"
"| `notification_send` tool                         | Yes (by target / subject)  | Interrupt for subjects that need a device ring |\n"
"| Chat unread rise                                 | No                         | Yes                                            |\n"
"| Pomodoro phase end                               | No                         | Yes                                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:38
msgid ""
"Do **not** merge “remind else due” into a single Inbox write. Due and "
"advance reminders are different products."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time discovery (Habitat): sleep-until-next"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Target:** discover due / reminder fire times with an **in-process sleep-until-next** loop. Do **not** use the PG cron job table (`builtin-task-reminders`, `cron_jobs` / `cron_log`) for this path.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:44
msgid "Semantics:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loop:\n"
"  process all already-due dues and reminders\n"
"  query earliest next fire time\n"
"  if none → disarm; wake again on task mutation\n"
"  else arm a single timer for that delay\n"
"  on fire → process → reschedule\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Rule             | Detail                                                                                                                                                                 |\n"
"| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| How many timers? | **At most one** next-fire arm — not one timer per timed row                                                                                                            |\n"
"| Implementation   | Equivalent to `while { work; sleep(next) }` on the Habitat event loop via **one** delayed timer (e.g. `setTimeout`); do not block the process with a synchronous sleep |\n"
"| On mutation      | Creating/patching `due_at` / reminders **cancels and recomputes** the next wake                                                                                        |\n"
"| Empty idle       | No cron_log spam; stay asleep until the next real fire or a mutation                                                                                                   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:62
msgid ""
"Other builtins (sleep cycle, env-health, user Agent cron jobs) may keep the "
"existing cron-table machinery. This aspect only moves **task due / reminder "
"discovery** off that path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:64
msgid ""
"Portal must **not** poll Inbox or task lists to implement attention. See "
"[page refresh](page-refresh.md) “Limited auto”."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delivery: WebSocket, not Portal polling"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Stage                | Mechanism                                                                                                                               |\n"
"| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Time discovery       | Habitat in-process sleep-until-next                                                                                                     |\n"
"| Push to Portal       | Existing Habitat RPC **WebSocket** events                                                                                               |\n"
"| Known local deadline | Optional `scheduleLocalAlert` (e.g. pomodoro); when companion is visible, prefer the immediate path (OS timers cannot drive the bubble) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart LR\n"
"  Mut[\"task due or reminder change\"] --> Arm[\"recompute one next timer\"]\n"
"  Boot[\"Habitat boot\"] --> Arm\n"
"  Arm -->|\"sleep until next\"| Fire[\"process due subset\"]\n"
"  Fire -->|\"due\"| Inbox[\"Notification\"]\n"
"  Fire -->|\"advance reminder\"| Ev[\"WS reminder event\"]\n"
"  Fire --> Arm\n"
"  Inbox --> Shell[\"shell Attention\"]\n"
"  Ev --> Shell\n"
"  Shell --> Alert[\"deliverLocalReminder\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where listening lives (Attention hub)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer                         | Owns                                                                                                                            | Does not own                   |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n"
"| Habitat sleep-until-next      | Time discovery; due → Inbox; advance reminder → event                                                                           | Portal UI                      |\n"
"| Habitat RPC session (one WS)  | Durable link; all `subscribe*` pumps bound to the **same** session map (abort on disconnect)                                    | Per-feature second sockets     |\n"
"| **Shell Attention (central)** | Main-window AppFrame (or one portal-sdk entry): ensure subscriptions while connected; route events; call `deliverLocalReminder` | Module list UIs                |\n"
"| Module handlers (registered)  | Map chat / inbox / pomodoro / future task-reminder events → `LocalReminderInput`                                                | Own WebSocket or list polling  |\n"
"| Companion overlay             | Render bubble via shell IPC                                                                                                     | Inbox / reminder bus subscribe |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:97
msgid ""
"Main window close is hide-not-destroy on desktop; shell subscriptions should "
"keep running while the process lives."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:99
msgid ""
"Today `PomodoroShellWatcher`, `ChatUnreadShellWatcher`, and "
"`NotificationReminderShellWatcher` sit side by side on AppFrame with "
"duplicated connect gates — target is one Attention registration surface; "
"refactor is follow-up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Module map (target)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Event                              | Notification        | Local interrupt                             |\n"
"| ---------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Task due                           | Yes (World subject) | Via inbox created and/or explicit interrupt |\n"
"| Task advance reminders             | No                  | Yes (direct)                                |\n"
"| Agent / system `notification_send` | Yes                 | Per product (user rows typically interrupt) |\n"
"| Chat unread rise                   | No                  | Yes                                         |\n"
"| Pomodoro phase end                 | No                  | Yes                                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Current gaps (code vs this aspect)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:113
msgid "Documented so agents do not treat today’s behavior as the end state:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:119
msgid ""
"`builtin-task-reminders` (and sleep-cycle / env-health / temporal-summary-"
"tick) use **in-process `Bun.cron`** — not PG `cron_jobs` / `cron_log`. On "
"**any** failure (throw or `{ ok: false }`), Habitat writes Inbox to **both** "
"user and agent subjects (no run history otherwise). **Sleep-until-next** for "
"sparse task dues is still a follow-up (today still wakes every minute in-"
"process; empty task scans stay quiet)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:119
msgid ""
"Single `remind_at` field; scan uses **remind-else-due** and writes the "
"**user** Inbox for both — conflates Notification and Reminder, and ignores "
"World ownership."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:119
msgid "Scan only walks `user_world_id`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:119
msgid "Shell attention is three independent watchers, not one hub."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:119
msgid "No multi-reminder model (7d / 3d / 1d) yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/aspects/notification-and-reminder.md:121
msgid ""
"Inbox protocol, tools, and agent inject details remain in "
"[`notifications.md`](../cognition/notifications.md). Alert channel details "
"remain there under Alert / `deliverLocalReminder`."
msgstr ""

